# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GymX environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO database URLs, on purpose. This is the core of the tenancy safety model:
#
#   DATABASE_URL      Owner role, DIRECT endpoint. Migrations, bootstrap, seeds.
#                     Postgres does NOT apply row-level security to a table's
#                     owner, so the application must never use this connection.
#                     Must be the direct host — migrations take advisory locks
#                     and issue DDL, which a transaction-mode pooler breaks.
#
#   APP_DATABASE_URL  The `gymx_app` role, POOLED endpoint. Owns nothing, has
#                     BYPASSRLS off, subject to every policy. Everything the
#                     admin app and the jobs do goes through this.
#
# On Neon the two hosts differ by one substring:
#   direct  ep-xxx-123456.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech
#   pooled  ep-xxx-123456-pooler.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech
#
# IMPORTANT: create the gymx_app role with `pnpm db:bootstrap`, NOT through the
# Neon console. Console-created roles are granted neon_superuser, which carries
# BYPASSRLS and would silently defeat every policy in packages/db/sql/rls.sql.
# The bootstrap script refuses to continue if it detects this.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://neondb_owner:PASSWORD@ep-xxx-123456.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech/gymx?sslmode=require"
APP_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://gymx_app:APP_PASSWORD@ep-xxx-123456-pooler.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech/gymx?sslmode=require"

# Password assigned to the gymx_app role by `pnpm db:bootstrap`.
# Must match the password inside APP_DATABASE_URL above.
APP_DB_PASSWORD="change-me-to-something-long"

# Auth.js. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
AUTH_SECRET="replace-me-with-a-32-byte-base64-secret"
AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# Vercel Blob — member photos and documents (Phase 1 onwards).
# Create a Blob store in the Vercel dashboard and copy its read/write token.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=""

# Shared secret for POST /api/jobs/run, called on a schedule by
# .github/workflows/cron.yml. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
CRON_SECRET="replace-me-with-a-random-hex-secret"

NODE_ENV="development"
